{"parentUuid":"6ee69983-26fe-42b8-9401-0d929a28f984","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"367fc39b-12e2-463b-91e0-327488109c6b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GYMdvfaJa5Lh4nXQPKrPcf","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I now have comprehensive information. Let me compile my findings.\n\n## Research Findings: NanoClaw OpenAI/Codex Support\n\nBased on my research, here's what I found about installing and configuring NanoClaw with OpenAI Codex as an alternative to Claude:\n\n### What Changed to Support Codex\n\n**Release: v2.17 (June 17, 2026)**\nNanoClaw added official Codex (OpenAI) provider support through the `/add-codex` skill. The release notes state: \"New agent provider: Codex (OpenAI) — run `/add-codex`. Full runtime via `codex app-server` (planning, MCP tools, server-side history, resume).\"\n\nThis provides feature parity with the default Claude provider, including:\n- MCP tool access\n- Server-side message history\n- Session resume capabilities\n- Automatic token-based compaction at 40K input tokens\n\n### API Key Format & Authentication\n\nNanoClaw supports **two authentication methods** for Codex:\n\n1. **ChatGPT Subscription (Recommended for individuals)**\n   - Run `codex login` on the host after `/add-codex` installation\n   - Session authentication is isolated per-session via mounted auth files\n\n2. **API Key (Recommended for CI/production)**\n   - Set `OPENAI_API_KEY` environment variable in `.env`\n   - Also set `CODEX_MODEL` to specify the model\n   - API-based billing replaces subscription charges\n   - Note: If both subscription and API key are present, subscription takes priority\n\n### How the Installer Handles Provider Selection\n\nThe `nanoclaw.sh` installer process:\n1. Clones the repo: `git clone https://github.com/nanocoai/nanoclaw.git && cd nanoclaw && bash nanoclaw.sh`\n2. Runs an interactive wizard that defaults to Claude\n3. Users can \"pick **Codex** to install it inline and authenticate\" during setup\n4. Credentials are stored securely in the **OneCLI vault** (not in the container)\n5. If setup fails, Claude Code is automatically invoked for troubleshooting\n\n### Known Gotchas & Differences from Claude Setup\n\n**Configuration Differences:**\n- Claude uses Anthropic API keys (`sk-ant-api…` format) or OAuth tokens\n- Codex uses OpenAI API keys or ChatGPT subscription login\n- Credentials are managed identically (OneCLI vault), so security posture is the same\n\n**Custom OpenAI-Compatible Endpoints:**\n- Set `OPENAI_BASE_URL` for providers like Groq or Together (experimental)\n- This feature is marked as experimental and may require patching\n\n**Environment Variable Gotcha:**\n- When both ChatGPT subscription (auth.json) and `OPENAI_API_KEY` are set, the subscription takes priority\n- If using mixed setups, the Codex app-server may report \"API key configured\" even though subscription auth is active\n\n**Platform Limitations:**\n- Google Cloud VMs are known not to work\n- Requires macOS or Linux (WSL compatible) with 4GB+ RAM\n- Cannot run installer as root on Linux\n- 5-minute container timeout per security design\n\n**Provider Configuration:**\n- Configure per agent group in two locations:\n  - `groups/<folder>/container.json` → `\"provider\": \"codex\"`\n  - `agent_groups.agent_provider` → `'codex'`\n- Different agent groups can use different providers simultaneously\n\n### Sources\n\n- [NanoClaw Releases - v2.17](https://github.com/nanocoai/nanoclaw/releases)\n- [NanoClaw Codex Provider Skill Documentation](https://nanoclaw.dev/skills/codex/)\n- [NanoClaw Quick Start Guide](https://docs.nanoclaw.dev/quickstart)\n- [NanoClaw GitHub Repository](https://github.com/nanocoai/nanoclaw)\n- [GitHub Issue #1984 - Custom Endpoint Support](https://github.com/nanocoai/nanoclaw/issues/1984)\n- [Coder Legion Article - NanoClaw Codex Port](https://coderlegion.com/14496/we-ported-nanoclaw-from-claude-to-codex-the-hard-part-was-not-the-runtime)"}]}]},"uuid":"2f8f0dcf-8c54-4c94-9e69-239d9a338b52","timestamp":"2026-07-06T18:30:08.723Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Research how to install NanoClaw (nanoclaw.sh) on a server using the Codex (OpenAI) API instead of Claude/Anthropic. \n\nNanoClaw is an open-source AI agent platform (see https://github.com/nanoclawai/nanoclaw or similar). It has a `nanoclaw.sh` installer that sets up the agent on a VPS. Recently (around June 2026) they added support for OpenAI/Codex as an alternative to Claude.\n\nPlease:\n1. Check the NanoClaw GitHub repository for any mention of Codex/OpenAI provider support\n2. Check the NanoClaw community Discord or documentation for Codex installation guides\n3. Look for blog posts or guides about installing NanoClaw with Codex/OpenAI\n4. Check https://nanoclaw.com or similar official sites\n\nThe goal is to understand:\n- What changed to support Codex\n- What API key format is needed (OpenAI key vs Anthropic key)\n- How the installer (nanoclaw.sh) handles provider selection\n- Any known gotchas or differences from the Claude setup\n\nReport findings concisely - what you found and where.","agentId":"a868848502bbe5820","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I now have comprehensive information. Let me compile my findings.\n\n## Research Findings: NanoClaw OpenAI/Codex Support\n\nBased on my research, here's what I found about installing and configuring NanoClaw with OpenAI Codex as an alternative to Claude:\n\n### What Changed to Support Codex\n\n**Release: v2.17 (June 17, 2026)**\nNanoClaw added official Codex (OpenAI) provider support through the `/add-codex` skill. The release notes state: \"New agent provider: Codex (OpenAI) — run `/add-codex`. Full runtime via `codex app-server` (planning, MCP tools, server-side history, resume).\"\n\nThis provides feature parity with the default Claude provider, including:\n- MCP tool access\n- Server-side message history\n- Session resume capabilities\n- Automatic token-based compaction at 40K input tokens\n\n### API Key Format & Authentication\n\nNanoClaw supports **two authentication methods** for Codex:\n\n1. **ChatGPT Subscription (Recommended for individuals)**\n   - Run `codex login` on the host after `/add-codex` installation\n   - Session authentication is isolated per-session via mounted auth files\n\n2. **API Key (Recommended for CI/production)**\n   - Set `OPENAI_API_KEY` environment variable in `.env`\n   - Also set `CODEX_MODEL` to specify the model\n   - API-based billing replaces subscription charges\n   - Note: If both subscription and API key are present, subscription takes priority\n\n### How the Installer Handles Provider Selection\n\nThe `nanoclaw.sh` installer process:\n1. Clones the repo: `git clone https://github.com/nanocoai/nanoclaw.git && cd nanoclaw && bash nanoclaw.sh`\n2. Runs an interactive wizard that defaults to Claude\n3. Users can \"pick **Codex** to install it inline and authenticate\" during setup\n4. Credentials are stored securely in the **OneCLI vault** (not in the container)\n5. If setup fails, Claude Code is automatically invoked for troubleshooting\n\n### Known Gotchas & Differences from Claude Setup\n\n**Configuration Differences:**\n- Claude uses Anthropic API keys (`sk-ant-api…` format) or OAuth tokens\n- Codex uses OpenAI API keys or ChatGPT subscription login\n- Credentials are managed identically (OneCLI vault), so security posture is the same\n\n**Custom OpenAI-Compatible Endpoints:**\n- Set `OPENAI_BASE_URL` for providers like Groq or Together (experimental)\n- This feature is marked as experimental and may require patching\n\n**Environment Variable Gotcha:**\n- When both ChatGPT subscription (auth.json) and `OPENAI_API_KEY` are set, the subscription takes priority\n- If using mixed setups, the Codex app-server may report \"API key configured\" even though subscription auth is active\n\n**Platform Limitations:**\n- Google Cloud VMs are known not to work\n- Requires